A **savings goal calculator** tells you exactly how long it will take to accumulate a target amount given your starting balance, regular monthly savings, and the interest earned on your savings. For Australians saving a house deposit, an emergency fund, or a large purchase, understanding the timeline is critical to staying motivated and choosing the right savings vehicle — whether a high-interest savings account, term deposit, or offset account.

As of May 2026, the best Australian high-interest savings accounts (HISAs) are offering **4.5–5.5% per annum**, subject to conditions such as monthly deposit requirements or limiting withdrawals. On a $150,000 deposit target starting from $20,000 with $2,500 in monthly savings at 4.5%, the goal is reached in approximately 4 years and 4 months, with interest contributing around $15,000 of the final balance. This calculator also shows the monthly savings amount needed to reach your goal within 2 years, helping you reverse-engineer your budget.
